# auth.env - credentials for the web UI (and an RTSP attempt that doesn't work - read on).
#
# Copy this file to "auth.env" (same directory) and fill in real values to turn ON
# authentication. Leave a value blank, or delete/rename auth.env entirely, and that part stays
# OPEN (no login) - exactly like it was before this feature existed. Nothing here is read unless
# this exact file ("auth.env", without ".example") exists on the SD card.
#
# WEB_USER / WEB_PASS: HTTP Basic auth for the whole web UI (busybox httpd), the whole site
#                       (/, /cgi-bin/*, recordings, player.html, config.html - everything).
#                       This one works - confirmed on hardware.
#
# RTSP_USER / RTSP_PASS: NOT ACTUALLY ENFORCED - confirmed on hardware (see docs/13-auth.md).
#                         rtspd does pick these up and calls the SDK's own Digest-auth setup
#                         with them (needs a one-time rtspd rebuild), but vs0/vs1 stay playable
#                         with no credentials at all regardless - the vendor's closed
#                         librtsp_server.so doesn't appear to actually gate the live-stream URLs
#                         with it in this build. Left here in case that's ever worth revisiting,
#                         but don't rely on it for anything - keep RTSP (port 554) off the
#                         internet/untrusted networks instead.
#
# auth.env itself is never committed to git (see .gitignore) - only this .example file is.

WEB_USER=
WEB_PASS=

RTSP_USER=
RTSP_PASS=
